title: t/00-load.t does not know File::SOPS::Metadata::Flat
updated: 2026-08-21T09:12:31Z
---

t/00-load.t lists the distribution's modules, and File::SOPS::Metadata::Flat is
not among them -- it has been missing since the module was added. Noticed while
adding File::SOPS::Comment to that list in karr #147; not taken along, because
the Metadata lane is working in that module right now.

Note what the position in the file decides. Every use_ok after use_ok('File::SOPS')
loads a module File::SOPS has already pulled in, so it can no longer fail: the
load was already proven (or already fatal) one line earlier. That is why the
Comment entry sits FIRST, with a comment saying so. A Metadata::Flat entry has
the same property -- File::SOPS::Metadata loads it -- so decide deliberately
whether the entry is meant as a list item or as a real check of standalone
loadability, and place it accordingly.

Lane: test.
